/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (In villages and cities across Tamil Nadu, people continue to lose their lives due to electrical infrastructure failures. One of the most dangerous situations occurs when an overhead power line snaps and falls to the ground while still carrying live current. People, livestock, and wildlife may unknowingly come into contact with the conductor, resulting in severe electric shock, permanent injury, or death.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (Current protection systems such as fuses, Miniature Circuit Breakers \(MCBs\), Ground Fault Protection \(GFP\), and other conventional protective devices do not always detect small breaks in branch conductors or partial wire snaps. As a result, a broken live conductor may remain energized for a significant period before authorities become aware of the hazard.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
