192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (The recurring electrocution incidents reported across Tamil Nadu demonstrate that existing protection mechanisms and administrative interventions alone are insufficient to eliminate the risk posed by snapped conductors and electrical leakage. The proposed Adaptive Electrical Hazard Intelligence Network introduces a proactive, AI-driven framework capable of detecting, analyzing, predicting, and reporting hazardous electrical conditions before they result in injury or loss of life. By shifting from fault response to hazard prevention, the system has the potential to significantly improve public electrical safety across both urban and rural environments.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
